Skip setup.py's own iOS cross-compile block when EXTRA_CMAKE_ARGS is set.

20261020 added a cibuildwheel-oriented iOS block that swaps the compilers for
raw `xcrun clang++` and re-derives the SDK, deployment target and Python paths.
forge's compiler wrappers carry the simulator `-target`; raw clang++ does not,
so the simulator slice compiles for iOS-simulator but links as iOS:
"ld: building for 'iOS', but linking in object file ... built for
'iOS-simulator'". The recipe already passes every setting that block sets
through EXTRA_CMAKE_ARGS, so let the recipe's own args stand alone.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -118,7 +118,8 @@
                     sysconfig.get_config_var("LDLIBRARY"),
                 )),
             ]
-        elif sys.platform == "ios":
+        elif sys.platform == "ios" and not os.environ.get("EXTRA_CMAKE_ARGS"):
+            # mobile-forge: skipped when the caller passes its own cross args
             # use the selected target python framework and native xcode compilers
             # cross-venv compiler wrappers may otherwise select the host macos sdk
             arch, sdk = sys.implementation._multiarch.rsplit("-", 1)
